    "hint": "Por simetría radial, $\\bar{x} = \\bar{y} = 0$. Calcule $M_{xy} = \\iiint z \\, dV$ en coordenadas esféricas y divida entre el volumen del hemisferio $\\frac{2\\pi R^3}{3}$.",
    "solution": "1. **Momento estático $M_{xy}$ en esféricas:**\n$$z = \\rho\\cos\\varphi, \\quad dV = \\rho^2 \\sin\\varphi \\, d\\rho \\, d\\varphi \\, d\\theta.$$\n$$M_{xy} = \\int_0^{2\\pi} d\\theta \\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\cos\\varphi\\sin\\varphi \\, d\\varphi \\int_0^R \\rho^3 \\, d\\rho.$$\n- $\\int_0^{2\\pi} d\\theta = 2\\pi$.\n- $\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\cos\\varphi\\sin\\varphi \\, d\\varphi = \\left[ \\frac{\\sin^2\\varphi}{2} \\right]_0^{\\pi/2} = \\frac{1}{2}$.\n- $\\int_0^R \\rho^3 d\\rho = \\frac{R^4}{4}$.\n$$M_{xy} = 2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{R^4}{4} = \\frac{\\pi R^4}{4}.$$\n\n2. **Cálculo de $\\bar{z}$:**\n$$\\bar{z} = \\frac{M_{xy}}{V} = \\frac{\\frac{\\pi R^4}{4}}{\\frac{2\\pi R^3}{3}} = \\frac{3}{8} R.$$",
